      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This raises the crucial point of subjective intent, which weakens the pure \"strict scrutiny\" argument in practice. To address this, pivot your argument toward institutional safeguards, asserting that while perfect clarity is impossible, courts must develop rigorous, objective legal tests—such as the *Goldwater* standard—to adjudicate these claims. Frame the stability argument not as protecting the powerful, but as preventing the arbitrary weaponization of the subpoena power, thereby ensuring both branches respect constitutional boundaries.",
